  "battle_rhythm": "It and its rider or mount are in perfect battle rhythm: the higher Speed for both, +2 AC, Advantage on Dexterity saving throws, difficult terrain ignored, no Opportunity Attacks from movement; once a turn, after one hits, the other may move 10 feet or Shove as a Reaction.",
  "beauty_motion": "Beauty in Motion When you move at least 10 feet on your turn, you may spend 1 cultivation points (your Path resource) to leave a trail of graceful motion until the start of your next turn. During this time, the first creature that makes an Opportunity Attack against you must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the Opportunity Attack misses automatically. On a successful save, the attack is made with Disadvantage.",
  "bell_rung": "Bell-Ringer (Berserker): Disadvantage on Intelligence saving throws while it lasts; the talent's Intelligence-check and Concentration-save-specific disadvantage are GM-only riders.",
  "bitter_edge": "Bitter Edge: its first hit each turn deals extra Cold damage.",
  "black_vein_palm_choice": "Black-Vein Palm — Black Vein When you use Ruin Channel on an unarmed strike, fist, palm, claw, spear-hand, or other Internal Channel, increase the Ruin Channel bonus damage by 1d8. If the attack hits a creature, choose one: - the target cannot regain HP until the start of your next turn; - the target has Disadvantage on the next Constitution saving throw it makes before the end of its next turn; - the target cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn. After resolving the attack, gain 1 Black Vein Strain.",
  "blade_fist_choice": "CL3 - Blade Fist Your unarmed strikes may deal Slashing damage and gain the Finesse property. You may use Dexterity instead of Strength or Constitution for Iron Fist attack and damage rolls. While wielding a Blade weapon: - Use Dexterity or Constitution for its attack and damage rolls. - If using Constitution, use your Cultivation Attack Modifier. - It is integrated into your Body Refining cultivation. - Refined Iron Fist and Heavenly Fist apply to it. Once per turn when you hit with an unarmed strike or integrated Blade weapon, choose one: - Deal additional Slashing damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus. - Reduce the target's Speed by 5 feet until the start of your next turn. - Prevent it from taking Reactions until the start of its next turn. - Draw or stow one Blade weapon. Normalized Procedure — Blade Fist - A Blade is a dagger, sword, saber, cutting-edged axe, or weapon carrying the Blade tag. Record each integrated Blade weapon. - Granting Finesse to your unarmed strikes permits Strength or Dexterity under the weapon-property rule; this feature additionally permits Constitution through Iron Fist. Choose one ability for each attack and add it once. - While wielding an integrated Blade, choose Dexterity or Constitution for each attack. Choosing Constitution uses the Cultivation Attack Modifier. The weapon retains its normal item statistics and tags. - Refined Iron Fist and Heavenly Fist apply their cultivation-powered and high-authority weapon benefits to the integrated Blade; they do not add a second Iron Fist damage die. - The once-per-turn rider is chosen after a hit. The additional Proficiency Bonus damage is one packet of Slashing damage. The Speed reduction does not stack with itself. Reaction denial lasts as printed. Drawing or stowing one Blade is part of the hit rider and does not create another object interaction. - An unarmed strike dealing Slashing damage remains an unarmed strike and natural bodily attack; it does not become a held Blade weapon for a feature requiring one.",
  "bleeding": "Black Thorn Demon Body's Bleeding: no automatic per-turn damage (unlike burning); it ends early and deals Proficiency Bonus damage the first time the bearer willingly moves a cumulative 10 feet or makes an attack. Your Game Master resolves it.",
  "blinded": "It can't see, and fails any ability check that needs sight. Its attack rolls have Disadvantage. Attack rolls against it have Advantage.",
  "blood_puppet": "A Blood Puppet's puppeteer chooses one command at the start of each of its turns: move it up to half its Speed toward the puppeteer or away from it, make it fall Prone, prevent it from taking Reactions, set its Speed to 0 until the end of that turn, or force it to drop what it holds.",
  "blossom_anchored": "A Traveling Garden's thorned field moves with it. An unwilling bearer repeats a Wisdom save at the end of each of its turns; a success ends the anchor.",
  "blossom_carried": "A dormant Blossom of the Flowers sphere rides it (a faint spiritual flower). Its maker may make it bloom; it withers in an hour, and this creature can use an Action to remove it.",
  "blossom_false_death_used": "A Flower of False Death has already kept it standing; it cannot again until the next long rest.",
